usible but unproven cardiac involvement)"], "excluded_candidates": ["CML chronic phase (elevated LAP contradicts typical Ph-negative low-LAP profile)", "Reactive causes (chronic symptoms weaken acute viral-induced leukemoid reaction candidacy)", "Lymphoproliferative disorder (normal differential excludes lymphocytosis patterns like CLL)"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss, fatigue, and abdominal pain (systemic constitutional signs)", "Elevated white cell count (66.5 × 10⁹/L) with normal differential (suggests clonal non-lymphoid proliferation)", "Leukocyte alkaline phosphatase elevation (Tier 2 high-risk marker for myeloid neoplasms)", "Mild hypertension (150/100 mmHg) and low-grade fever (37.5°C) with no localized infection"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.8663101604278074, "posterior": 0.42509541984732824, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP and normal differential exclude CML (B1.1) due to its low LAP feature, indirectly moderately support MPN-NOS (B1.2) as a diagnosis, and are neutral for lymphoproliferative disorders (B2) and reactive leukocytosis (B3)"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly does not rule out MPN-NOS (B1.2) as per WHO 2022 criteria which permits this finding, but it mildly weakens B1 as a diagnostic family compared to alternatives. B2 remains unaffected."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of gradual blood count abnormalities", "Presence of splenomegaly or hepatomegaly"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy with cytogenetics", "Ph chromosome detection", "JAK2/V617F mutation testing"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.019879134860050888, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of monoclonal immunoglobulin symptoms (normal liver/kidney tests, no Bence Jones proteinuria) decisively excludes multiple myeloma (B2) despite systemic constitutional symptoms; however, other lymphoproliferative subtypes remain possible though unsupported by current evidence."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.039758269720101776, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.038645038167938926, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["A prior CML diagnosis is required for chronic-phase CML, and its absence with normal differential does not support this diagnosis."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Phase Transformation (CML in Blast Crisis)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.17326203208556148, "posterior": 0.05152671755725191, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Preserved differential and lack of prior CML history are atypical for Blast Crisis but not definitively incompatible with WHO 2022 criteria.", "The absence of blasts in a complete workup with normal differential strongly suggests against Blast Crisis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Clinical history of subacute splenomegaly/constitutional symptoms", "Presence of basophilia or undiagnosed BCR-ABL1 positivity"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow 