usible but unproven cardiac involvement)"], "excluded_candidates": ["CML chronic phase (elevated LAP contradicts typical Ph-negative low-LAP profile)", "Reactive causes (chronic symptoms weaken acute viral-induced leukemoid reaction candidacy)", "Lymphoproliferative disorder (normal differential excludes lymphocytosis patterns like CLL)"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss, fatigue, and abdominal pain (systemic constitutional signs)", "Elevated white cell count (66.5 × 10⁹/L) with normal differential (suggests clonal non-lymphoid proliferation)", "Leukocyte alkaline phosphatase elevation (Tier 2 high-risk marker for myeloid neoplasms)", "Mild hypertension (150/100 mmHg) and low-grade fever (37.5°C) with no localized infection"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.8663101604278074, "posterior": 0.42509541984732824, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP and normal differential exclude CML (B1.1) due to its low LAP feature, indirectly moderately support MPN-NOS (B1.2) as a diagnosis, and are neutral for lymphoproliferative disorders (B2) and reactive leukocytosis (B3)"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly does not rule out MPN-NOS (B1.2) as per WHO 2022 criteria which permits this finding, but it mildly weakens B1 as a diagnostic family compared to alternatives. B2 remains unaffected."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of gradual blood count abnormalities", "Presence of splenomegaly or hepatomegaly"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy with cytogenetics", "Ph chromosome detection", "JAK2/V617F mutation testing"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis"